# Syntax error messages by parser state; ANVIL_PARSER_STATE=1 prints the state.

# top level
cunit: XOR
cunit: KEYWORD_ENUM IDENT LEFT_BRACE IDENT RIGHT_BRACE XOR
cunit: KEYWORD_PROC IDENT LEFT_PAREN RIGHT_PAREN LEFT_BRACE RIGHT_BRACE XOR
cunit: KEYWORD_CONST IDENT EQUAL INT SEMICOLON XOR
cunit: KEYWORD_IMPORT STR_LITERAL XOR
cunit: KEYWORD_FUNCTION IDENT LEFT_PAREN RIGHT_PAREN LEFT_BRACE BIT_LITERAL RIGHT_BRACE XOR
cunit: KEYWORD_CHAN IDENT LEFT_BRACE RIGHT_BRACE XOR

expected a top-level definition
help: a file contains `proc`, `chan`, `type`, `struct`, `enum`, `func`, `const` and `import` definitions

# cycle n
cunit: KEYWORD_FUNCTION IDENT LEFT_PAREN RIGHT_PAREN LEFT_BRACE KEYWORD_CYCLE XOR

expected a number of cycles after `cycle`
help: the number of cycles is an integer literal, a parameter or a constant, e.g. `cycle 3` or `cycle N`

# generate (i : start, end, step) and generate_seq
cunit: KEYWORD_FUNCTION IDENT LEFT_PAREN RIGHT_PAREN LEFT_BRACE KEYWORD_GENERATE_SEQ LEFT_PAREN IDENT COLON XOR
cunit: KEYWORD_FUNCTION IDENT LEFT_PAREN RIGHT_PAREN LEFT_BRACE KEYWORD_GENERATE_SEQ LEFT_PAREN IDENT COLON INT COMMA XOR
cunit: KEYWORD_FUNCTION IDENT LEFT_PAREN RIGHT_PAREN LEFT_BRACE KEYWORD_GENERATE_SEQ LEFT_PAREN IDENT COLON INT COMMA INT COMMA XOR
cunit: KEYWORD_FUNCTION IDENT LEFT_PAREN RIGHT_PAREN LEFT_BRACE KEYWORD_GENERATE LEFT_PAREN IDENT COLON XOR
cunit: KEYWORD_FUNCTION IDENT LEFT_PAREN RIGHT_PAREN LEFT_BRACE KEYWORD_GENERATE LEFT_PAREN IDENT COLON INT COMMA XOR
cunit: KEYWORD_FUNCTION IDENT LEFT_PAREN RIGHT_PAREN LEFT_BRACE KEYWORD_GENERATE LEFT_PAREN IDENT COLON INT COMMA INT COMMA XOR

the start, end and step of `generate` must be integer literals
help: e.g. `generate (i : 0, 7, 1) { ... }`

# set r := v
cunit: KEYWORD_FUNCTION IDENT LEFT_PAREN RIGHT_PAREN LEFT_BRACE KEYWORD_SET IDENT XOR

expected `:=` after the register in `set`
help: registers are assigned with `:=`, e.g. `set r := 8'd1`

# endpoint.message
cunit: KEYWORD_FUNCTION IDENT LEFT_PAREN RIGHT_PAREN LEFT_BRACE KEYWORD_SEND IDENT XOR

expected `.` and a message name after the endpoint
help: a message is named as `endpoint.message`, e.g. `recv ep.req`

# send ep.msg (v)
cunit: KEYWORD_FUNCTION IDENT LEFT_PAREN RIGHT_PAREN LEFT_BRACE KEYWORD_SEND IDENT PERIOD IDENT XOR

expected the value to send in parentheses
help: e.g. `send ep.req (8'd1)`

# dprint "..." (args)
cunit: KEYWORD_FUNCTION IDENT LEFT_PAREN RIGHT_PAREN LEFT_BRACE KEYWORD_DPRINT STR_LITERAL XOR

expected the values to print in parentheses after the format string
help: e.g. `dprint "x = %d" (x)`, or `dprint "done" ()` when there is nothing to print

# *r
cunit: KEYWORD_FUNCTION IDENT LEFT_PAREN RIGHT_PAREN LEFT_BRACE ASTERISK XOR

expected a register name after `*`
help: `*` reads a register, e.g. `*r`

# e1; e2
cunit: KEYWORD_FUNCTION IDENT LEFT_PAREN RIGHT_PAREN LEFT_BRACE BIT_LITERAL SEMICOLON XOR

expected an expression after `;`
help: `e1; e2` starts both expressions at the same time; remove the `;` if nothing follows it

# e1 >> e2
cunit: KEYWORD_FUNCTION IDENT LEFT_PAREN RIGHT_PAREN LEFT_BRACE BIT_LITERAL DOUBLE_GT XOR

expected an expression after `>>`
help: `e1 >> e2` starts `e2` once `e1` has finished; remove the `>>` if nothing follows it

# reg r : type;
cunit: KEYWORD_PROC IDENT LEFT_PAREN RIGHT_PAREN LEFT_BRACE KEYWORD_REG IDENT XOR

expected `:` and a type after the register name
help: e.g. `reg r : logic[8];`

# chan c { left m : (...), ... }
cunit: KEYWORD_CHAN IDENT LEFT_BRACE XOR
cunit: KEYWORD_CHAN IDENT LEFT_BRACE KEYWORD_LEFT IDENT COLON LEFT_PAREN RIGHT_PAREN COMMA XOR

expected a message definition
help: a message starts with its direction, `left` or `right`, e.g. `left req : (logic[8]@#1)`

cunit: KEYWORD_CHAN IDENT LEFT_BRACE KEYWORD_LEFT IDENT COLON XOR

expected the message type in parentheses
help: e.g. `left req : (logic[8]@#1)`
